@bsipocz why Table is "better" than pandas (the question comes up regularly)

@taldcroft We should have a FAQ, but for the record (and for your tutorial), Table provides these capabilities that are not in pandas DataFrame:

* Robust support for table and column metadata. This is needed for representing data in file formats like FITS and VOTable.
* Support for N-dimensional column data, for example a table of thumbnail images in a source catalog.
* Support for columns of astropy Time, Quantity, and SkyCoord / Frame objects.
* General support for external "mixin" columns, for instance dask arrays.

